{
  "hookSpecificOutput": {
    "hookEventName": "PreToolUse",
    "additionalContext": "EHL pre-edit checks — from briefing.html (scoring) and CHECKLIST.md (Entire gate). Check this edit against them before writing:
1. Clean clone must still run — the highlights agent scores would_it_run.
2. Keep the free metadata points: README, tests, Dockerfile.
3. Boilerplate ratio 0.3-0.5 — delete scaffolding you do not use rather than leaving it in.
4. Git activity must read normal — commit roughly every 30 min with a real message, never one large dump.
5. Echo the brief vocabulary in README, headings and commit messages.
6. Never break .claude/settings.json, .entire/ or the git hooks — that is the Entire submission gate.
7. Target 5-7 on the rubric. Avoid a 3; do not spend hours chasing a 9."
  }
}
